definition.message:
{{#is_alert}}
Device **{{device_name.name}}** on `{{catalyst_center_host.name}}` has been unreachable from Catalyst Center for 10 minutes.

1. Check [reachability by site](/metric/explorer?exp_metric=cisco_catalyst_center.device.reachable&exp_scope=catalyst_center_host:{{catalyst_center_host.name}}&exp_group=site_hierarchy&exp_agg=avg&exp_type=line). If other devices at the same site are also down, suspect the site (uplink, WAN, or power) rather than the device.
2. Open the device in [Catalyst Center](https://{{catalyst_center_host.name}}/). **Ping Reachable** means it is up but SNMP or NETCONF is failing; **Unreachable** means no response at all.
{{/is_alert}}

{{#is_recovery}}
Device **{{device_name.name}}** on `{{catalyst_center_host.name}}` is reachable again.
{{/is_recovery}}
